@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: how cmd/proveo/main.go gets from 3505 lines to under 1000 without changing what it does
' covers: cmd/proveo/main.go
' covers: internal/egress/**
' covers: internal/sbx/**
'
' ── MEASURED TODAY (script over top-level declarations) ─────────────────────
'   cmd/proveo/main.go      3505 lines, 158 top-level declarations
'   doRun                    569 lines — one function, every decision in the run
'   sbx backend             ~798 lines — sandboxSpec, runSandbox, Kit, secrets, MCP
'   prompt + posture rows   ~311 lines — choiceui gating, header, transcript rows
'   credential resolution   ~286 lines — broker, auth suppression, .env, gh token
'   docker+egress execution ~218 lines — execWithEgress, sidecar logs, review gate
'   cobra wiring            ~187 lines — main, runCmd, setup, projects, clean
'   the rest               ~1150 lines — pty/tail plumbing, glyphs, small helpers
'
' ── THE FOUR PATTERNS, AND WHY EACH ONE ─────────────────────────────────────
' 1. STRATEGY over the two backends. `doRun` branches on sbxBackend and then keeps
'    both worlds' locals alive in one scope. A Backend interface — Plan(RunSpec)
'    then Execute(Plan) — lets each live in its own package with its own tests, and
'    makes "which backend ran" a value rather than a flag read six times.
' 2. PIPELINE of named stages over one RunSpec. doRun is already a sequence:
'    resolve workspace → resolve credentials → prompt → posture → select → execute →
'    teardown. Written as stages, each is independently testable and the order is
'    visible in ten lines instead of inferred from 569.
' 3. PURE PLAN / IMPURE APPLY, generalised. sandboxSpec is pure and runSandbox holds
'    the effects; that split is what makes --print faithful. Every stage adopts it:
'    a stage returns a value, one executor applies it. --print then costs nothing to
'    keep honest, because it IS the plan.
' 4. VALUE OBJECT for the posture. observability, enforcedBy, imagePosture,
'    workspacePosture, mcpGatewayPosture and rolesLine each answer one row and are
'    called from two places. One Posture type renders the prompt header and the
'    transcript block from the same fields — the drift this session found (a row
'    naming Squid logs on a backend that runs none) becomes unrepresentable.
'
' ── TARGET LAYOUT ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   cmd/proveo/main.go            ~250   cobra wiring, flags, main()
'   cmd/proveo/commands.go        ~200   run/setup/projects/clean/version subcommands
'   internal/run/spec.go          ~150   RunSpec, runParams, resolution helpers
'   internal/run/stages.go        ~250   the pipeline, one function per stage
'   internal/run/backend.go        ~80   Backend interface + selection
'   internal/backend/dockeregress  ~320   assemble, execWithEgress, sidecar logs
'   internal/backend/sandbox       ~700   sandboxSpec, runSandbox, Kit, secrets
'   internal/posture               ~250   the rows, rendered once for two readers
'   internal/credentials           ~300   broker set, auth suppression, .env, gh
'   internal/agentio                ~200   pty proxy glue, tail writer, stdin trace
'
' ── SEQUENCE — six moves, each compiles and ships on its own ────────────────
'   0. DONE — cmd/proveo/golden_test.go + cmd/proveo/testdata/plan/*.golden pin the
'      rendered plan of BOTH backends: the agent argv, every sidecar/network/cleanup
'      command, the sbx argv, the Kit spec.yaml and the secret NAMES (never values,
'      asserted). Six docker cases x tier/credentials/local-model/shell, three sbx.
'      Regenerate with `go test ./cmd/proveo -run Golden -update`, and read the diff:
'      every move below is behaviour-preserving, so a changed golden is the bug.
'      Proven non-vacuous by injecting one env var and watching it go red.
'   1. DONE — internal/agentio holds Stdio, Tail, Tracer, FilterEnabled and the three
'      TTY predicates (_spec/internal/agentio/agent-terminal-io.puml). main.go 3505 →
'      3311; six tests moved with the code, plus new cover for FilterEnabled and the
'      TTY predicates. Goldens unchanged, which is the proof the move was inert.
'      Two pre-existing breaks surfaced and were repaired on the way: the integration
'      suite did not COMPILE (Options.Provider became Providers []string at the
'      multi-provider change) and then asserted PROVEO_EGRESS_PROVIDER= without the S.
'      A suite that cannot compile is a suite that cannot fail — the same drift class
'      as _spec/_plans/revision-env-egress.puml.
'   2-6. Written out with their symbol inventories, seams, risks and proofs in
'        _spec/_plans/main-decomposition-moves.puml. Move 6 is gated on a readable
'        e2e baseline — _spec/_plans/restore-green-e2e.puml.
'
' ── CONSTRAINTS THAT SHAPE IT ───────────────────────────────────────────────
'   * internal/contract.TestInternalPackagesDoNotImportRoot — the embedded manifest
'     FS must be PASSED IN, never imported by a new internal package.
'   * --print must stay a pure function of the spec, or move 4 and 5 lose their test.
'   * runlog.Fields is written from one place today; posture keeps that property.
title PLANNED — cmd/proveo/main.go 3505 → under 1000, by composition rather than by cutting

component "cmd/proveo\nmain · cobra commands · flags" as CLI <<host>>

frame "internal/run — the pipeline" as RUN <<host>> {
  component "RunSpec\nresolved, immutable input" as SPEC <<db>>
  component "stages\nworkspace · credentials · prompt ·\nposture · select · execute · teardown" as STAGES <<app>>
  component "Backend\nPlan(RunSpec) → Plan\nExecute(Plan) → error" as IFACE <<app>>
}

frame "backends — one strategy each" as BE <<host>> {
  component "internal/backend/dockeregress\nsidecars · MITM · Squid · review gate" as DOCKER <<app>>
  component "internal/backend/sandbox\nKit · secrets · sbx run · policy log" as SANDBOX <<app>>
}

frame "extracted collaborators" as COLL <<host>> {
  component "internal/posture\nthe rows, rendered once" as POSTURE <<app>>
  component "internal/credentials\nbroker set · auth suppression · .env" as CREDS <<app>>
  component "internal/agentio\npty proxy · tail · stdin trace" as AGENTIO <<app>>
}

component "doRun — 569 lines\nevery decision in one scope" as GOD <<error>>

CLI ARROW_MAIN SPEC : parse flags into one value
SPEC ARROW_MAIN STAGES
STAGES ARROW_MAIN CREDS
STAGES ARROW_MAIN POSTURE
STAGES ARROW_MAIN IFACE : select, do not branch
IFACE ARROW_MAIN DOCKER
IFACE ARROW_MAIN SANDBOX
DOCKER ARROW_QUEUE AGENTIO
SANDBOX ARROW_QUEUE AGENTIO
GOD ARROW_ERROR STAGES : what this replaces

note bottom of GOD
  Workspace resolution, provider detection, the
  choice form, the transcript, both backends and
  teardown share one scope — so a change to any of
  them is a change to all of them, and the only
  test covering it end to end needs Docker.
end note

note bottom of IFACE
  Two backends already exist in fact; only the
  type is missing. Naming it turns "which one ran"
  into a value the posture reads, instead of a
  bool read in six places and forgotten in a
  seventh.
end note

note bottom of POSTURE
  This session found a row promising Squid logs on
  a backend that runs no Squid, two lines under a
  row that said so. One type rendering both
  readers makes that contradiction
  unrepresentable.
end note

note bottom of SPEC
  Pure in, pure out: --print renders the same
  value the run executes. sandboxSpec already
  works this way, and it is the property that
  keeps a dry run worth trusting.
end note

note bottom of AGENTIO
  Lifted first because it depends on nothing else
  in the run: pty proxy glue, the tail writer that
  keeps the last lines of a failed agent, and the
  stdin tap.
end note
@enduml
